  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Browser profile enumeration (Chrome / Edge / Brave / Firefox)", "technique": "T1555.003", "what_happened": "At 2033-10-04 15:18:08 UTC on WS-SALES-22, AMSI EID 4104 captured a powershell.exe scriptblock iterating Test-Path on browser profile paths: $env:LOCALAPPDATA\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Default, ...\\Microsoft\\Edge\\User Data\\Default, ...\\BraveSoftware\\Brave-Browser\\User Data\\Default, $env:APPDATA\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Profiles.", "chain_reason": "Enumerating multiple browser profile paths in one scriptblock is the precondition step of T1555.003 — the attacker maps which browsers are installed before extracting their credential stores."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Login Data + Local State copy from Chrome profile to user Temp", "technique": "T1555.003", "what_happened": "At 2033-10-04 15:18:22, Sysmon EID 11 captured creation of C:\\Users\\e.koval\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p134_chrome_151808\\Login_Data.sqlite (294 KB SQLite) AND C:\\Users\\e.koval\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p134_chrome_151808\\Local_State.json (28 KB). Both copied from C:\\Users\\e.koval\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Default\\Login Data + Local State. Rule 61611 triggered.", "chain_reason": "Chrome's Login Data SQLite contains every URL+username+encrypted-password the user has saved. Local State contains os_crypt.encrypted_key (the DPAPI-encrypted Chrome master key). Together they enable offline decryption of every saved Chrome credential. Copying to user Temp (not corp backup destination) is unambiguous theft."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Parse Local State.json for os_crypt.encrypted_key (DPAPI decryption preparation)", "technique": "T1555.003", "what_happened": "At 2033-10-04 15:18:38, AMSI EID 4104 captured a powershell.exe scriptblock invoking ConvertFrom-Json on Local_State.json AND extracting $ls.os_crypt.encrypted_key field. The scriptblock then computes [Convert]::FromBase64String($encKey) and logs the raw byte length + ASCII prefix ('DPAPI'). Rule 92400 triggered.", "chain_reason": "os_crypt.encrypted_key in Chrome's Local State is a Base64-encoded blob prefixed with 'DPAPI' (5 bytes) + the DPAPI-encrypted AES key. To decrypt every saved password the attacker calls ProtectedData.Unprotect on the bytes after the 'DPAPI' prefix using the current user's DPAPI master key."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Cookies + Web Data + History copy + tool literals", "technique": "T1555.003", "what_happened": "At 2033-10-04 15:18:52, Sysmon EID 11 captured copies of Chrome\\\\Default\\\\Cookies (148 KB), Web Data (412 KB), History (812 KB) to the same user Temp directory. AMSI EID 4104 captured scriptblock literals: 'SharpChromium.exe full', 'mimikatz.exe \"dpapi::chrome /in:Login Data /unprotect\"', 'lazagne.exe browsers --output cleartext', 'Get-WebBrowserPassword (PowerSploit)', 'firefox_decrypt.py'.", "chain_reason": "Cookies = session tokens for any active webmail/SaaS/banking session = direct hijack opportunity. Web Data = autofill data including credit cards. History = browsing surveillance. The 5 tool literals show full T1555.003 toolkit awareness — operator-style attack notes."}
